# Dashboard Panels

## Telemetry Health — Reporting Hosts

### Purpose

Identify systems currently sending events to Splunk and determine when each host last reported.

### SPL

```spl
index=*
| stats count as events latest(_time) as last_event by host
| convert ctime(last_event)
| sort host
```

### Analyst Use

Unexpected absence of a normally active host may indicate:

- Powered-off system
- Splunk Forwarder issue
- Network connectivity problem
- Endpoint failure
- Logging configuration problem

---

## Telemetry Status

### Purpose

Provide a simplified operational classification of telemetry freshness.

### SPL

```spl
index=*
| stats latest(_time) as last_event by host
| eval age_seconds=now()-last_event
| eval status=case(
age_seconds<=300,"HEALTHY",
age_seconds<=900,"DELAYED",
true(),"STALE")
| convert ctime(last_event)
| table host last_event status
| sort host
```

### Status Model

| Age | Status |
|---|---|
| ≤ 300 seconds | HEALTHY |
| 301–900 seconds | DELAYED |
| > 900 seconds | STALE |

These are lab-defined thresholds.

---

## Security Telemetry by Event Type

### Purpose

Display volume for security-relevant Windows telemetry.

### SPL

```spl
index=* (EventCode=4624 OR EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4104 OR EventCode=4698 OR EventCode=4728)
| eval telemetry=case(
EventCode=4624,"Successful Logon",
EventCode=4625,"Failed Logon",
EventCode=4104,"PowerShell",
EventCode=4698,"Scheduled Task",
EventCode=4728,"Group Membership Change",
true(),"Other")
| stats count by EventCode telemetry
| sort EventCode
```

---

## Failed Authentication by Account

### Purpose

Identify accounts generating Windows authentication failures.

### SPL

```spl
index=* EventCode=4625
| stats count as failed_logons by TargetUserName
| sort - failed_logons
```

### Analyst Review

Investigate unexpected concentrations of failures involving:

- Administrative accounts
- Service accounts
- Dormant accounts
- Unusual usernames
- Repeated failures followed by successful authentication

---

## Remote Network Logons

### Purpose

Monitor successful network authentication from non-local source addresses.

### SPL

```spl
index=* EventCode=4624 LogonType=3
| where IpAddress!="-" AND IpAddress!="127.0.0.1" AND IpAddress!="::1"
| stats count as network_logons by TargetUserName IpAddress
| sort - network_logons
```

### Detection Relationship

This panel uses the same foundational telemetry associated with:

```text
DET-006
```

and:

```text
CORR-002
```

